Author: Melan <m.khamdannn91@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 9 21:58:09 2026 +0700

    Surface journal-posting failures instead of swallowing them

    postExpenseJournal, postPurchaseJournal, and the utang-payment RPC call
    in purchases/actions.ts all called supabase.rpc("post_journal_entry", ...)
    without checking the result — if posting ever failed (e.g. a renamed or
    missing account code), the expense/purchase/payment row would still save
    while the journal silently ended up incomplete, with Neraca still
    reporting "seimbang" despite the gap. Now the error is checked, logged
    as a warning activity entry, and returned to the form so the user knows
    the record saved but needs a manual correcting journal entry.

